 "reading": "T1 passes every pre-registered check on the untouched 2007-2015 gold history. Paper research only: at most a candidate for a forward paper record, by the owner's decision; nothing live changes. 2007-15: +0.111R a trade net (n 1657, month t +3.19), gross +0.203R (t +5.96); 2007-11 +0.120R (n 929), 2012-15 +0.100R (n 728); at 2x costs +0.018R; 40 of 40 placebo seeds beaten (placebo median −0.031R). Costs take 0.092R a trade at a median stop of $7.76. Pooled 2007 → 2026-11-12: +0.073R net (n 3713, month t +3.35), gross +0.155R (t +7.24). High-range days (previous range above its 250-day median) 2007-15 −0.015R (n 682), low-range +0.199R (n 975); descriptive only. Cautions, said plainly: the cost is the original's fixed $0.60 a round trip, today's level; spreads of 2007-15 were not measured, and at 2x costs the rule keeps only +0.018R a trade (pooled 2007-26 −0.009R). The record is two good stretches with a flat one between: 2015-2024 together +3.25R on 1883 trades. The gain does not come from wide-range days; it comes from days after a narrower-than-usual range. A pass here is evidence for the rule's direction on gold, not proof of a tradeable edge at real costs. "
